    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "greater",
     "smaller",
     "ascending",
     "descending"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "To compare numbers, compare the thousands first, then hundreds, tens and ones.\nThe digits 3 and 7 can make 333, 337, 373, 377, 733, 737, 773 and 777. The smallest is 333 and the largest is 777.\nUsing 3, 5, 0, 8 we can form many numbers. A number cannot start with 0.\nAscending means smallest to largest. Descending means largest to smallest.\nWhich number is greater: 4,215 or 4,251? Thousands same, hundreds same, tens 1 and 5, so 4,251 is greater."
    }
   },
